==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*seh₁p-}}
From {{bor|en|mul|Homo sapiens}}, from {{der|en|la|sapiēns}}, present active participle of {{m|la|sapiō||discern, be capable of discerning}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sapiens}}

# A [[human being]] (''{{ll|mul|Homo sapiens}}'').
#* {{quote-book|en|title=How we got to be human: subjective minds with objective bodies|page=277|author=William H. Libaw|year=2000|passage=The earliest '''sapiens''' were gatherers, scavengers, and hunters of food.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Classification and Human Evolution|page=335|author=Sherwood L. Washburn|year=2005|passage=Even if we assume that the rate of change was slow and the evolving population large, we must still assume that '''sapiens''' was rather isolated.}}

